out/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/server/target/
logs/
# The hosted world and its per-start backups (tools/serve.sh).
var/

# Captures: ignored in bulk, with one curated exception.
#
# A capture is the only artefact this project cannot regenerate -- it is a
# recording of a real client, taken on a machine with a real installation,
# and no amount of reasoning reproduces one. The whole archive was ignored
# and therefore untracked, unbacked-up and present on exactly one disk: one
# `rm -rf`, or a fresh clone, and the lot was gone.
#
# So `captures/regression/` is tracked and the rest is not. The tracked set
# is small and chosen: enough to replay against the server as a regression
# test, including one capture that holds a bug we have since fixed, because a
# recording of the failure is worth more than the memory of it.
captures/*
!captures/regression/

# Scratch files that are not part of the project (client log dumps, one-off
# captures pasted in while debugging). Nothing here is ever committed.
tmp/

# Claude Code session state (scheduled-task locks and the like). Harness
# bookkeeping for whoever is driving the session, not project content.
.claude/

# patch(1) leftovers: a fuzzed coordinator-diff apply once committed one (review V1)
*.orig
*.rej
